# Triple lock — sports picks & results

**Default:** every sport’s **predictions** and **results** pages are locked.
Agents must not edit them unless the owner says exactly:

**UNLOCK &lt;SPORT&gt;**

and names the miss. **One sport. One miss.**

## Locked surfaces (no unlock = no edits)

For every sport (MLB, NHL, NBA, NFL, NCAAF, NCAAB, NCAAW, WNBA, CFL,
soccer, tennis, UFC, golf, and any sport added later):

- `/&lt;sport&gt;-picks`, `/&lt;sport&gt;-results`, chart views
- Sport card HTML, Books/H2H/model face chips, Cards|Chart
- Sport-named modules whose job is that sport’s picks/results UI
- Sport-only branches in `NHL77FINAL.py` / `team_results_charts.py` /
  `templates/includes/game_card_body.html`

## Critical: unlocked work must not touch locked sports

Fixing **player props**, chrome, checkers, or an unlocked sport **must not**
edit locked sports’ picks/results pages or card faces — even “incidentally”
in shared files. If a shared edit would change locked sport B while sport A
(or props) is the task, stop and ask.

Shared blank-slate merge allow-lists may prevent empty slates only — never
rewrite another sport’s Books / face / model chips.

## Props is not a sports unlock

`/player-props` and the props eligibility stack may be edited when the owner
asks to fix props. That is **not** an unlock for NFL/MLB/etc. picks or results.

## When done with an unlock

Lock that sport again in `.cursor/rules/locked-&lt;sport&gt;.mdc`. Do not leave
sports UNLOCKED overnight.

Also follow: `one-miss-only.mdc`, `sport-lock-enforcement.mdc`, AGENTS.md Rule 12.
